  "_about": "Who lives in Riverwood, who works or drinks where, and who gets on with whom. Hand-written from vanilla Skyrim; check and edit freely. People are matched by their Skyrim.esm base form ID, so names here are only for reading. gossipy is 0..1 (0.5 = average) and sets how readily someone passes news on; it is the only personality trait the simulation reads today, and it is written only the first time a person is seeded. Children (Frodnar, Dorthe) are left out on purpose: Living World never includes child NPCs.",
  "_communities_about": "kind is one of settlement, household, faction, guild. Gossip treats every 'household' as a group whose members see each other daily (high contact), so the inn and the mill use that kind for the people who work or spend their days there, not because they are families. role is a plain description. influence is meant as social standing (how much others weigh this person's views), not ownership or authority; nothing reads it yet. Nobody's opinion is set by a community: each person forms their own from what they see and hear.",
