  "_romance_about": "Romance traits (Living World romance, flag MANTELLA_LW_ROMANCE=1). 0..1, 0.5 = average. romantic: how much they seek romance. drive: interest in physical intimacy. monogamy: how firmly they keep to one partner (low = may stray). jealous: how hard a partner's interest elsewhere hits them. flirtatious: how readily they flirt, even when taken. shy: holds them back from asking. modesty: how private a place must feel. trusting and loyal: how readily they forgive. attracted_to: sexes they can be attracted to (edit freely; vanilla gives no orientation, so these default to the other sex). intimacy_boundary: never, married_only, committed_only, after_courtship or casual_ok, the least bond they need before any intimacy. Gerdur and Hod are tuned on purpose: Hod is curious and flirts with other women; Gerdur keeps to him less firmly and his flirting hurts her, so she is the likeliest in Riverwood to stray. Nobody is ever forced: every encounter still needs both people's own yes.",
